[{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/3504646424","html_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/pull/112035#issuecomment-3504646424","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/112035","id":3504646424,"node_id":"IC_kwDOAO6SJc7Q5KkY","user":{"login":"Ivorforce","id":2308167,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjIzMDgxNjc=","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/2308167?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/Ivorforce","html_url":"https://github.com/Ivorforce","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Ivorforce/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Ivorforce/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Ivorforce/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Ivorforce/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Ivorforce/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Ivorforce/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Ivorforce/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Ivorforce/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Ivorforce/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2025-11-07T19:59:45Z","updated_at":"2025-11-07T20:21:44Z","body":"> Tested this PR a bit and came to a realization: we can simplify the number of functions even further! Because the tag-syntax operator simply calls to a default allocator, we can simply call the allocation function new instead.\r\n\r\nI don't think we should do this.\r\n\r\nWith a tag parameters, the `new` implementation has a compile-time static call path (to `Memory::alloc_static`). This is simple and predictable.\r\n\r\nUsing the function pointer `new` function, it's using a `void*` parameter, which compiles to a dynamic call. Dynamic calls can be substantially slower[^1] than compile-time static calls, because may not be predicted correctly, causing cache misses and branch mispredictions.\r\nOf course, we expect this to be 'optimized away', but that can only happen if the `new` operation is inlined (also, god knows if MSVC would manage). Which means that we'll take a significant penalty in dev builds, and possibly longer compile times because we're expecting more work from the optimizer.\r\nAll in all, this is not a risk i'd be willing to take, considering the alternative is just to have the additional `new` overload.\r\n\r\n[^1]: https://www.agner.org/optimize/optimizing_cpp.pdf","author_association":"MEMBER","reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/3504646424/reactions","total_count":0,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"performed_via_github_app":null,"minimized":null},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/3504722456","html_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/pull/112035#issuecomment-3504722456","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/112035","id":3504722456,"node_id":"IC_kwDOAO6SJc7Q5dIY","user":{"login":"Repiteo","id":17489292,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE3NDg5Mjky","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/17489292?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/Repiteo","html_url":"https://github.com/Repiteo","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Repiteo/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Repiteo/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Repiteo/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Repiteo/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Repiteo/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Repiteo/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Repiteo/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Repiteo/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Repiteo/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2025-11-07T20:15:31Z","updated_at":"2025-11-07T20:15:31Z","body":"In that case, I'll rescind that specific suggestion (though the rest of the suggestions stand). It'd be nice if we could just have the allocator unilaterally passed for alloc like we do with the freeing equivalents, but that's obviously a much bigger undertaking","author_association":"CONTRIBUTOR","reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/3504722456/reactions","total_count":0,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"performed_via_github_app":null,"minimized":null},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/4281302596","html_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/pull/112035#issuecomment-4281302596","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/112035","id":4281302596,"node_id":"IC_kwDOAO6SJc7_L35E","user":{"login":"Ivorforce","id":2308167,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjIzMDgxNjc=","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/2308167?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/Ivorforce","html_url":"https://github.com/Ivorforce","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Ivorforce/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Ivorforce/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Ivorforce/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Ivorforce/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Ivorforce/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Ivorforce/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Ivorforce/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Ivorforce/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Ivorforce/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2026-04-20T13:47:14Z","updated_at":"2026-04-20T14:03:50Z","body":"(i rebased since t